WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.350
Speaker 1: You guys know that phrase.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.540
When it rains, it pours.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:10.299
It just won't stop pouring for Donald Trump's
former lawyer, Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:10.299 --> 00:00:16.350
There's a new report that Rudy Giuliani reportedly
called an Arizona official about getting the

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:23.460
election challenge, quote, fixed up so that
Donald Trump would win Arizona back during

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.770
the 2020 election.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:30.440
Now, remember that flipping Arizona alone
would not have given Donald Trump the presidency

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.830
anyway.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.220
Remember that Rudy Giuliani is already under
a major investigation.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.680
His home and his office were raided just a
few weeks ago.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.680
And now this.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:47.510
The Arizona Republic revealed on Sunday that
Rudy Giuliani called the Maricopa County supervisor,

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:52.000
Bill Gates, not the Microsoft guy, just a
guy with the same name on Christmas Eve of

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.780
2020 to introduce himself as the lawyer for
Donald Trump.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.140
He left an incredible message.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.480
It's almost mafia like about getting this
situation resolved for everybody.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.640
Check out this quote.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.060
The Arizona newspaper obtained the audio and
published a transcript.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.280
Rudy left a message saying, quote, Bill, it's
Rudy Giuliani, President Trump's lawyer.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.850
If you get a chance, would you please give
me a call?

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.689
I have a few things, a few things I'd like
to talk over with you.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:20.600
Maybe we can get this thing fixed up.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.360
You know, I really think it's a shame that
Republicans sort of are both in this kind

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.369
of situation.

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:33.299
And I think there may be a nice way to resolve
this for everybody.

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.130
Why does every Rudy Giuliani quote throughout
this entire thing sound like something you'd

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.490
expect to hear on The Sopranos?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.710
Not from the lawyer to a sitting president
of the United States?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.909
The difference is, I would imagine that a
real mobster wouldn't leave a message like

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:52.939
this on a phone with their real name and speaking
so explicitly about what it is that they want.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:58.689
It would be, you know, someone shows up at
the house of this Maricopa County supervisor

00:01:58.689 --> 00:02:04.459
and says, hey, our friend in DC says he wants
to talk about the Arizona thing and get it

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:05.469
fixed up.

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:06.530
You understand?

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.830
But no, Rudy just does it.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.310
He does it without any hesitation.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.120
He just does it via voicemail.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.780
And Gates has since been asked about the voicemail
and said, I never returned Rudy's call explaining

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.210
that, quote, We don't do what is easy.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.710
We do what is right.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.560
What's scary about that is the implication
that it would have been easy to just flip

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.360
the results and give the state to Trump.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.870
I hope that's not what Supervisor Gates actually
means here.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:36.240
Now, many of you have been emailing me regularly
saying, how is Rudy not in jail already?

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.080
There are many answers to that question.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.690
The first is people like Rudy don't tend to
go to jail.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:47.700
We have a two tiered justice system and people
like Rudy tend not to end up in jail or in

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.700
prison.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.950
Second is that the investigation that's currently
ongoing was significantly obstructed by Trump

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.760
appointees to the Justice Department when
Trump was president.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.820
They are now coming out and saying Biden got
Rudy's home and office raided.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:06.210
No, actually, the investigation started when
Trump was still president and they tried to

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.500
get a search warrant all the way back then.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.870
But Trump appointees in the Justice Department
obstructed it and blocked it and prevented

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:13.870
it from happening.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.010
So this all would have happened under Trump
had Trump's loyalists in the Justice Department

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.890
not interfered.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.170
And third, I just don't think Rudy Giuliani's
going to prison, period.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:28.350
And whenever I say that people are angry or
people say, David, you should at least optimistically

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.930
say, let's hope Rudy goes to prison, OK?

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.870
If Rudy committed crimes for which he is found
guilty, I hope he's given prison time.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.530
That would be a that would be just after everything
that he's been involved in.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.350
I don't believe Rudy is going to prison.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.270
I don't believe Trump is going to prison.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:49.520
And so I'm not going to gaslight you and tell
you that I think that that's a realistic possibility,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.460
that that's just what it is.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.530
If you disagree, if you think that there's
some real way that Rudy Giuliani ends up in

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.530
prison.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:04:01.220
And to be perfectly frank, even if Rudy is
charged and doesn't plead out and is found

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:08.960
guilty at Rudy's age and for this type of
crime, I think that once you get to sentencing,

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.920
he doesn't get sent to prison anyway, even
with multiple guilty verdicts.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.220
I just don't see it.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.060
OK, if you disagree, let me know.

